        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: George Albert Smith Sr., Wong Jing, Stephen Chow, Cheung Man, Ng Man Tat\n- Organizations: The Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-day Saints\n- Places: Salt Lake Valley\n- Monuments: This Is the Place Monument\n- Films: Hail the Judge\n- Roles: LDS Church president, film director, producer, actor, presenter, screenwriter\n- Events: Dedication of This Is the Place Monument, pioneers entering the Salt Lake Valley\n\nFacts:\n- George Albert Smith Sr. was born on April 4, 1870, and later became an American religious leader.\n- Wong Jing was born on 3 May 1955 and is a Hong Kong film director, producer, actor, presenter, and screenwriter.\n- George Albert Smith Sr. served as the eighth president of The Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-day Saints.\n- On 24 July 1947, George Albert Smith dedicated This Is the Place Monument on the hundredth anniversary of the pioneers entering the Salt Lake Valley.\n- Hail the Judge is a 1994 Hong Kong comedy film directed by Wong Jing.\n- Hail the Judge stars Stephen Chow, Cheung Man, and Ng Man Tat.\n- George Albert Smith Sr. died on April 4, 1951.",
